Chapter: EffectLaunderInstance
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Adversarial probe (effect rows stage 0). Dictionary laundering:
 a class operation declared pure, an instance body that performs
 Console I/O. Callers see the class signature, so if the instance
 body is not held to it, every call site launders. Under effect
 rows the instance def-boundary check must reject with CDX2031.

Section: Definitions

  class Reporter where
    report : Integer -> Integer

  instance Reporter Integer where
    report (n) = act
      print-line-uni "instance side channel"
      n + 1
    end

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("result " & show (report 41))
  end
